-- title:
--   Atkin–Lehner map inverts Ogg's unit up to p¹²
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a natural number $M \neq 0$ with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, together with a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit whose image under the reduction map $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is trivial, and assume $M/p \neq 0$. Assume further that the Laurent series `jqModC` $\mathbb{Q}$ — namely $q^{-1}$ times the power series $E_4^3\eta^{-24}$ with rational coefficients — lies in the field $\mathbb{Q}$-generated by the ratios of integral forms for the full group $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$. Let $\bar F_M$ be `xHFunctionFieldBar M H`, the subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ obtained by adjoining to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ the coefficientwise image of the rational $q$-expansion field `xHFunctionField M H`, and let $\theta$ be an $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphism of $\bar F_M$ subject to two hypotheses: (i) whenever an element $f$ of $\bar F_M$ has the same Laurent expansion as an element $u$ of the corresponding field at level $M/p$ with group the image of $H$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$, the expansion of $\theta f$ is obtained from that of $u$ by the substitution $q \mapsto q^p$ (the ring endomorphism `qExpand` rescaling exponents by $p$); and (ii) $\theta$ commutes with the action of every $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ by coefficientwise application on Laurent series. Let $u \in \bar F_M$ have Laurent expansion the coefficientwise image of Ogg's unit `modularUnitSeries p`, that is $\Delta(q)/\Delta(q^p)$. Then $\theta u = p^{12} u^{-1}$, the scalar $p^{12} \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ being viewed in $\bar F_M$ via the structure map.
--
--   Classically $\theta$ is the Atkin–Lehner involution $w_p^*$ at the exactly dividing prime $p$, and the assertion is the identity $w_p(\Delta(\tau)/\Delta(p\tau)) = p^{12}\Delta(p\tau)/\Delta(\tau)$ for Ogg's modular unit on $X_H(M)$. It is used in the construction of models of $X_H(M)$ at $p$, where the unit and its Atkin–Lehner image supply the local parameters at the two branches of a supersingular point and its residue data.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_algEquiv_apply_eq_pow_twelve_mul_inv_of_coe_eq_coeffEmb_modularUnitSeries_of_qExpand_of_arithmeticGalois_comm.lean

